From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:27:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Do not leak the "system" sender name

gowhatsapp_display_text_message() set senderJid to g_strdup("system")
for a system message without a sender. senderJid is a local const
pointer, and nothing frees the copy, so every such message leaked it.
Point it at the literal instead.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 glue/display_message.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/glue/display_message.c b/glue/display_message.c
index e978cab..3953224 100644
--- a/glue/display_message.c
+++ b/glue/display_message.c
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ void gowhatsapp_display_text_message(
     
     if (flags & PURPLE_MESSAGE_SYSTEM) {
         if (senderJid == NULL) {
-            senderJid = g_strdup("system"); // g_strdup needed since senderJid is freed by caller
+            senderJid = "system";
         }
         gboolean bridge = purple_account_get_bool(account, GOWHATSAPP_BRIDGE_COMPATIBILITY_OPTION, FALSE);
         if (bridge) {
-- 
